<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paraguay</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Paraguayan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paraguay is a landlocked country in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>. In the 1860s it fought a devastating war against the Triple Alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a>. For the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguayan-war">Paraguayan War</a> of 1864–1870 transformed the army into a professional institution with political ambitions that later helped bring down the monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paraguay.jpg" alt="Paraguay" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Republica del Paraguay · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Paraguay.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
